name":"Ego softening"},{"name":"Sweating/chills"},{"name":"Muscle tension"},{"name":"Confusion"},{"name":"Insomnia"}],"combinations":[{"substance":"Amphetamines","status":"Unsafe","tone":"danger","note":"Documented unsafe interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"AMT","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Cocaine","status":"Unsafe","tone":"danger","note":"Documented unsafe interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Dxm","status":"Unsafe","tone":"danger","note":"Documented unsafe interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"MAOIs","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"PCP","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Tramadol","status":"Unsafe","tone":"danger","note":"Documented unsafe interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"2C-T-x","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"2C-x","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Cannabis","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"DOx","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"MDMA","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Mescaline","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Nbome","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."}],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"PsychonautWiki","description":"Pharmacology, subjective effects, and dosage reference","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/5-MeO-MiPT"},{"title":"TripSit Factsheet","description":"Rapid harm-reduction summary and combination data","url":"https://drugs.tripsit.me/5-meo-mipt"},{"title":"Erowid Experience Vaults","description":"First-person experience reports and archives","url":"https://www.erowid.org/experiences/subs/exp_5MeOMIPT.shtml"},{"title":"TiHKAL Entry","description":"Alexander & Ann Shulgin tryptamine monograph","url":"https://www.erowid.org/library/books_online/tihkal/tihkal40.shtml"},{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/5-MeO-MiPT"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on 5-MeO-MiPT","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4412834"},{"title":"維基百科","description":"zh:Encyclopedia article","url":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/zh-tw/5-MeO-MiPT"},{"title":"维基百科","description":"zh:Encyclopedia article","url":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/zh-cn/5-MeO-MiPT"}],"wikidata":"Q4412834","formula":"C15H22N2O","molarMass":246.35,"pharmacology":{"text":"The mechanism that produces the hallucinogenic effects of 5-MeO-MiPT is thought to result primarily from serotonin 5-HT2A receptor agonism combined with the 5-HT1A receptor activation. 5-MeO-MiPT also potently binds to 5-HT2B receptor with high affinity but low efficacy, 5-HT2C receptors with moderate potency, and displays sub-micromolar affinity towards multiple other serotonin receptors.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"5-MeO-MiPT","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/5-MeO-MiPT#Pharmacodynamics","kind":"Non-selective serotonin receptor agonist; Serotonin 5-HT2A receptor agonist; Serotonergic psychedelic; Hallucinogen; Entactogen","body":[{"what":"halfLife","says":"~2–3 hours"},{"what":"brokenDown","says":"CYP2D6"}],"figures":"5-MeO-MiPT"},"uses":{"text":"It is usually taken orally or smoked. The drug was encountered as a novel designer drug in 2004. Recreational use of 5-MeO-MiPT is significant but relatively rare.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"5-MeO-MiPT","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/5-MeO-MiPT","routes":"Oral, smoking","figures":"5-MeO-MiPT"},"sideEffects":{"text":"Adverse effects of 5-MeO-MiPT include loss of appetite and insomnia. It produced no meaningful cardiovascular or psychiatric adverse effects in a phase 1 clinical trial, including no anxiety. Low-dose 5-MeO-MiPT did not cause any serious histopathological effects on the liver, kidney, and brain. High doses induce apoptotic cell death through caspase activity especially in some parts of the organs.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"5-MeO-MiPT","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/5-MeO-MiPT#Side_effects"},"summaryZh":"5-MeO-MiPT是一種色胺衍生物，化學式為C15H22N2O，可作為致幻劑、迷幻藥物和宗教致幻劑。","summaryZhHans":"5-MeO-MiPT是一种色胺衍生物，化学式为C15H22N2O，可作为致幻剂、迷幻药物和宗教致幻剂。","ai":{"by":"Claude (Anthropic)","date":"2026-11-27","fact":{"en":"Its nickname moxy is a clipping of methoxy. Alexander Shulgin first made it and described it in TiHKAL, and it has since been tested in an early clinical trial.","zh":"它的暱稱「moxy」是「methoxy」的簡稱。Alexander Shulgin首次合成了它並收錄在《TiHKAL》中，後來它也進入了早期的臨床試驗。","zhHans":"它的暱称「moxy」是「methoxy」的简称。Alexander Shulgin首次合成了它并收录在《TiHKAL》中，后来它也进入了早期的临床试验。"}}}